{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.deuteron_chirality_regime_differs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.deuteron_chirality_regime_differs","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L152-L160","doc":"**The deuteron sits in a DIFFERENT chirality regime than the heavier light isotopes.** With\n`n = 3A`: `C(6,2) = 15` is ODD (A=2, deuteron → sgn antisymmetrizes conjugate pairs, bar-odd-projected)\nwhile `C(9,2) = 36` (A=3, T/³He) and `C(12,2) = 66` (A=4, ⁴He) are EVEN (sgn preserved). So the\ndeuteron's binding-sign structure is qualitatively unlike A ≥ 3 — a structural reason `C_knot(D)`\ncannot lie on the same universal curve as the heavier isotopes, independent of the mirror inequality\nabove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.sgn_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.sgn_conj","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L141-L150","doc":"**The conjugation law for the binding sign** (pure exponent arithmetic, no hypothesis needed):\n`(−1)^{n(λ')} = (−1)^{n(λ) + n(λ')} · (−1)^{n(λ)}`. With the Macdonald identity `n(λ) + n(λ') = C(n,2)`\nthis is `sgn(λ') = (−1)^{C(n,2)} · sgn(λ)` — the chirality regime is fixed by the parity of `C(n,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.no_writhe_only_framing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.no_writhe_only_framing","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L121-L128","doc":"**Writhe-only framing is excluded.** Since `writhe(D) = writhe(T) = 4`, any framing correction\nthat is a function of writhe alone (`C_knot = f(writhe)`, e.g. `q₀^{c·w}` — the omitted Jones/HOMFLY\nframing normalization) would force `C_knot(D) = C_knot(T)`. They differ, so no writhe-only factor\ncloses the deficit: `¬ ∃ v, C_knot(D) = v ∧ C_knot(T) = v` (both evaluated at the shared writhe 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.deuteron_triton_same_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.deuteron_triton_same_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L117-L119","doc":"**The deuteron and triton canonical words have equal writhe** `11 − 7 = 16 − 12 = 4` (`#σ − #σ⁻¹`;\naveraged interface crossings are writhe-neutral). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.CKnot_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.CKnot_T","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L114-L115","doc":"`C_knot(T)` — triton deficit; the triton word has the SAME writhe (4) as the deuteron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.CKnot_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.CKnot_D","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L111-L112","doc":"`C_knot(D)` — deuteron deficit (probe `c-knot-nonuniversal-pinned-weight.witness.json`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.mirror_gap_exceeds_isospin_band","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.mirror_gap_exceeds_isospin_band","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L91-L96","doc":"**The required rescales differ by more than the isospin band.** `C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) > 1.1`\n(measured 1.367), i.e. `B_T · S_He > 1.1 · (B_He · S_T)` — the mismatch a level-only closure would have\nto absorb exceeds the ~8% isospin tolerance (ROUTE 5), so the exclusion is not a marginal-precision\nartifact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.no_level_only_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.no_level_only_closure","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L81-L89","doc":"**No level-only rescale closes binding.** If a single scale `g` (`= g(9, q₀) · m_e`, the level-`H₉`\nvalue of any closure `B(K) = g(n_K, q₀) · m_e · S(K)`) reproduced BOTH the triton and the helion\nbinding from their `S` values, then `B_T · S_He = B_He · S_T`, contradicting `mirror_cross_ne`. Hence\n`C_knot` is not a function of `(n, q₀)` — it carries per-knot content. scope-(b) exclusion of the\nlevel-only-rescale closure class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.mirror_cross_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.mirror_cross_ne","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**The mirror-pair cross-inequality** `B_T · S_He ≠ B_He · S_T` — the cross-multiplied form of\n`C_knot(T) = B_T/S_T ≠ B_He/S_He = C_knot(³He)`. This is the structural obstruction to any level-only\nclosure: `T` and `³He` share the strand count `H₉`, so a rescale depending only on the level cannot\nreproduce both bindings. Falsifiable (a genuine numerical claim about the measured `(B, S)` pairs),\nsorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.B_He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.B_He","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L70-L71","doc":"AME 2020 binding of the helion `³He` (MeV) — experimental diagnostic target, never inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.B_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.B_T","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L67-L68","doc":"AME 2020 binding of the triton (MeV) — experimental diagnostic target, never inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.S_He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.S_He","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L64-L65","doc":"Master-formula magnitude `S(K)` for the helion `³He`, at the SAME `H₉`, pinned weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.S_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotNonUniversal.S_T","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotNonUniversal.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Master-formula magnitude `S(K) = |Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ(β_K) sgn f^λ|` for the triton, at `H₉`, with the\npinned Wenzl weight (probe `c-knot-nonuniversal-pinned-weight.witness.json`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}